"""Bodies, procedures and rights of the Atlas: references only.

Every legal statement is a reference to a provision, {"i": instrument, "a": article, "p": paragraph,
"x": phrase the provision must contain}; quotes.resolve() reads the wording from the official text and
the build fails if the phrase is not there. The short labels ("Quién puede presentarla", "Plazo")
are headings of the page, not statements of law: what each requirement is, is what the quoted
provision says. Procedures name the register data that tells whether a State has accepted them
(`acceptance`); the guide uses only that data and, when it is missing, says that it must be checked.
"""

def R(i, a, x=None, p=None):
    return {"i": i, "a": str(a), "x": x, "p": p}


